<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n7625" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Cestĭus</span></b> , ĭi,
			m., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>the name of a Roman plebeian family.</i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b> C. Cestius, <i><span class="en">Cic. Phil.
				3, 10, 26</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b> L. Cestius Pius, <i>a rhetorician of
			Smyrna</i>, <i><span class="en">Sen. Contr. 3</span></i>, prooem. p. 206, 3
			al.—Hence, <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Cestĭānus</span></b> , a, um,
				adj., <i>of</i> or <i>belonging to L. Cestius</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">color,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Sen. Contr. 1, 7, p. 125</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
